SalesView project rules:

1) Design system colors (must remain consistent):
- Background: #F1F5F9
- Card background: #FFFFFF
- Primary: #1E3A5F
- Positive metric: #10B981
- Negative metric: #EF4444
- Text primary: #0F172A
- Text secondary: #64748B
- Borders/separators: #E2E8F0
- Category bars:
  - Electrónica: #3B82F6
  - Ropa: #8B5CF6
  - Hogar: #F59E0B
  - Alimentos: #10B981
  - Deportes: #EF4444

2) Component architecture:
- Keep each UI component in its own file under src/components/.
- Current split: Header.jsx, PeriodFilter.jsx, KPICards.jsx, SalesTable.jsx, CategoryBreakdown.jsx.

3) Data source policy:
- Data is mocked and local-only.
- Always read from JSON files in /data (sales.json, team.json, config.json).
- Do not add backend, database, or external API calls.

4) Functional constraints (NO incluir):
- No login/authentication.
- No chart libraries (Chart.js, Recharts, D3, etc.).
- No PDF/Excel export.
- No dark mode.
- No real-time updates or external API integration.
- No data editing in the UI (read-only dashboard).
- No complex animations (only subtle CSS transitions).
- No routing/multiple pages (single-page view).
- No tooltips/popovers.
- No notifications/alerts.
- No footer.
